WEBVTT

NOTE calculation-methods: written VO text from episode.json, timed from the timeline VO placements

V0-1
00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:05.710
Two algorithms can produce
the suggested percentage.

V0-2
00:00:05.810 --> 00:00:08.600
They use different inputs
and behave differently.

V1a-1
00:00:12.850 --> 00:00:17.581
Suggested Percent Adjust Calculation is
the first field on the Calculation tab.

V1a-2
00:00:17.681 --> 00:00:22.592
On a production site it only appears when
the saved algorithm is already Option 1,

V1a-3
00:00:22.692 --> 00:00:24.310
so most users never see it.

V1b-1
00:00:24.866 --> 00:00:27.377
The dropdown offers only
Option 1 and Option 2.

V1b-2
00:00:27.477 --> 00:00:30.096
Nothing in the product
says what either one does.

V2a-1
00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:41.008
The default is Option 2:
delta plus today's ET.

V2a-2
00:00:41.108 --> 00:00:46.332
The server computes it per station.
Target minus working VWC gives a deficit,

V2a-3
00:00:46.432 --> 00:00:49.350
and the deficit becomes
an amount of water.

V2b-1
00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:54.265
Today's ET, adjusted by the
crop coefficient, is added,

V2b-2
00:00:54.365 --> 00:00:59.007
the daily maximum caps the total,
and the result is divided by the Lynx

V2b-3
00:00:59.107 --> 00:01:03.750
reference amount. Every suggestion
in this column came from that chain.

V3a-1
00:01:11.836 --> 00:01:15.309
Option 1 multiplies the
percent adjust Lynx currently

V3a-2
00:01:15.409 --> 00:01:19.144
holds by target divided by
measured moisture, and rounds.

V3a-3
00:01:19.244 --> 00:01:23.506
A station at 0 percent adjust
stays at 0 no matter how dry it is.

V3b-1
00:01:24.020 --> 00:01:26.768
It uses no ET, no reference
amount and no cap,

V3b-2
00:01:26.868 --> 00:01:31.290
so Max Amount and Lynx Reference Amount
are disabled while it is selected.

V4a-1
00:01:39.413 --> 00:01:43.811
Option 2 flattens everything above
the daily maximum onto one number.

V4a-2
00:01:43.911 --> 00:01:47.863
Runs of identical values are a
signature of the capped method.

V4b-1
00:01:48.413 --> 00:01:51.787
Option 1 has no ceiling,
so its suggestions spread out,

V4b-2
00:01:51.887 --> 00:01:56.243
and can go far higher than you intend
on a station that reads very dry.

V5a-1
00:02:03.316 --> 00:02:05.648
The algorithm is stored on the site,

V5a-2
00:02:05.748 --> 00:02:10.672
so a switch applies to every course on
the site, not just the one on screen.

V5a-3
00:02:10.772 --> 00:02:16.086
Saving a different algorithm recalculates
every station and reloads the dashboard.

V5b-1
00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:20.808
Review the whole Suggested column
before pushing anything after a switch.

V5b-2
00:02:20.908 --> 00:02:24.270
Compare the column before and
after switching, not one row.
